WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.560
Netflix offers so many options that choosing
the perfect thing to watch can be too much

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.680
to deal with.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.280
Here's a look at some of the best stuff to
add to your queue for the next time you don't

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.400
know what to watch on Netflix.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.880
What if John Wick was more violent, more nihilistic,
and with a gleeful undercurrent of shock humor

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.689
and an honest exploration of the mental effects
of a violent life?

00:00:20.689 --> 00:00:25.550
That's Polar, the messy story of one man's
quest to relax and secure his pension.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:30.119
Mads Mikkelsen, the Danish actor best known
for his starring role on the stylish TV version

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:35.170
of Hannibal, stars as Duncan Vizla, a highly
effective assassin forced by his corporate

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.290
bosses to retire at age 50 and enjoy his golden
years.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:42.060
Of course, his company plans to kill him off
to avoid funding his payout.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.460
From a lovely cabin in Montana, Duncan has
to fight off some violent attacks while also

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:51.160
dealing with PTSD and forging a friendship
with a neighbor with demons of her own.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.680
Groundhog Day may seem like a comedy, but
it's actually a horror movie.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.960
Seriously: A guy is such a nasty person that
the universe spontaneously conspires to make

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.489
him shape up by sticking him in a time loop
from which he cannot escape.

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:05.300
That's a living nightmare.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.040
ARQ takes Groundhog Day for the horror movie
it is and runs with it.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.970
Robbie Amell stars as an engineer responsible
for a world-changing technology, only to find

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:18.520
himself dealing with a home invasion brought
on by bad dudes who want his technology for

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:19.520
their own means.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.990
Our protagonist gets stuck in a time loop,
forcing him to experience his horrible situation

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:27.130
over and over again, until he can find a way
out.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.130
"Today is repeating.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.130
Tell me you remember.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:32.270
Come on, you have to remember."

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.600
"Have you lost your f---ing mind?"

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:42.550
Life in an especially dingy and crime-filled
part on London is rough for Tom, a shy and

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:46.252
awkward teenager who just wants to go about
his business and maybe take things to the

00:01:46.252 --> 00:01:47.820
next level with his friend Lucy.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.850
When he goes over to her apartment to study
together, he's greeted by thugs who have just

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.640
savagely attacked Lucy and her brother.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.460
Tom runs away and tries to call the police,
only for the thugs to shoot him in the head

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.770
and leave him for dead.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.880
The good news: He survived!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.700
The bad news: He wakes up two days after the
attack with bits of his phone stuck inside

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.300
in his severely damaged noggin.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.250
Luckily, like some kind of Silicon Valley
Spider-Man, the advanced computing technology

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:16.190
in the phone merges with Tom's brain to give
him superpowers.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:20.480
With those great powers, he takes it as his
responsibility to track down the bad guys

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.160
who nearly killed Lucy.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:27.840
Based on a Stephen King novel from the early
'90s, Gerald's Game begins like those countless

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:32.129
"erotic thrillers" that populated late-night
cable TV in that era: Married couple Gerald

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:35.590
and Jessie go away for a sexy weekend in a
cabin in the woods.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.959
But nothing good ever happens to people in
a Stephen King story.

00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:43.489
They engage in some increasingly troublesome
bedtime play which suddenly ends when Gerald

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:46.990
dies of a heart attack while Jessie remains
cuffed to the bed.

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:51.849
With very little hope of escape or rescue,
Jessie's mind rears up to attack her, presenting

00:02:51.849 --> 00:02:54.730
numerous hallucinations that feel real.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.400
Gerald's Game more or less takes place all
in one room, making the horror that much more

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.769
intense and palpable.

00:03:00.769 --> 00:03:05.090
The film creates an intimacy and emotionally
powerful connection with Jessie as the horror

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:06.090
unfolds.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:10.389
"'Cause everyone's got a little corner in
there somewhere.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.080
A little button they won't admit they want
pressed."

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:20.870
What if Baby Driver wasn't a soundtrack-driven
action comedy, and was instead an unpredictable,

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:25.099
intricately plotted suspense thriller about
a getaway driver having his worst ever day

00:03:25.099 --> 00:03:26.099
at work?

00:03:26.099 --> 00:03:30.610
That's the logline for Wheelmsan, which also
feels like the greatest Jason Statham movie

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.200
that Statham never made.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:37.040
Frank Grillo portrays the unnamed, unflappable
wheelman in a bank heist scheme, just out

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.909
of prison and in debt to a Boston crime family.

00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:43.970
Everything that could go wrong does, but it's
not all that funny, it's stressful enough

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:47.920
driving a getaway car for a robbery, and it's
even more nerve-wracking for the wheelman

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.250
when he gets more or less carjacked by another
band of mysterious criminals.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:56.329
Much of the action takes place inside the
car and inside the head of the wheelman, speeding

00:03:56.329 --> 00:03:59.560
along from one high-pressure situation to
another.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:04.240
James Badge Dale plays Clyne, one of the smartest
people in the world.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:09.040
Clyne is a DARPA scientist employed by the
U.S. military to develop weapons technology

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.980
to use in the ongoing Moldovan War in Eastern
Europe.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:16.280
He's summoned to the front lines to consult
on some strange findings captured by one of

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.320
his best gadgets, hyper-spectral goggles.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:23.760
It would seem some troops wearing the goggles
spotted some ghostly figures out in the wild

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:26.170
that tend to kill whatever they come in contact
with.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:30.570
Before the military can report to their higher-ups,
they need Clyne to figure out just what it

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:35.170
is, and so off he goes into the war zone to
stalk the beast alongside a special ops team

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.840
and a C.I.A. operative.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:40.720
What they find is way worse and more complicated
than they thought possible.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:46.100
A harrowing war movie with elements of District
9 and Predator thrown in, Spectral is clever,

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.800
intense, and worth a watch.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:52.640
Yes, there's a sequel to 2000's Crouching
Tiger, Hidden Dragon.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:57.510
And, like so many other revivals of classic
properties, it's just hanging out on Netflix.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:02.350
Loosely based on the same "Crane-Iron" series
of books by Wang Dulu as the original Crouching

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:07.610
Tiger, Sword of Destiny builds on its predecessor's
magical combination of folk tales, multi-faceted

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:10.920
characters, and physically impossible acrobatic
fight scenes.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:15.850
Michelle Yeoh returns as You Shu Lien, fresh
out of exile and locked in an important battle

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:19.630
with the West Lotus clan for control of the
Green Destiny sword.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.880
Directing Sword of Destiny is Woo-Ping Yuen,
the martial arts choreographer on the first

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:27.910
Crouching Tiger, and he certainly brings his
prowess for creating gorgeous and soaring

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.120
aerial combat sequences.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:35.320
Snowpiercer is one of the most original, thoughtful,
and unpredictable science fiction movies in

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:36.390
recent memory.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:41.030
The film takes place in a dystopian near future,
in which some malfunctioning technology has

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:44.990
triggered a new ice age and killed almost
all life on Earth.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:50.330
The humans that survive board Snowpiercer,
a gigantic super train that never stops circling

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.520
the entire planet.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:56.500
By 2031, the onboard society has split into
the wealthy, who get the luxury cars in the

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:01.310
front of the train, and the impoverished who
are forced to eat food cubes and live in subhuman

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:02.870
conditions in the tail.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:07.090
Rebels living in the tail of the train lead
a revolt after people living in the front,

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.720
led by the spooky Minister Mason, go too far.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.270
It all gets even more chaotic and compellingly
strange from there.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:16.310
"I am a hat, you are a shoe.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.480
I belong on the head, you belong on the foot.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.560
Yes?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.240
So it is!"

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:27.040
Why are period horror films so much scarier
than ones set in modern day?

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:31.680
Is it because the relative ignorance and brutality
of the past adds an extra element of terror?

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:36.710
Or are images of Victorian-era Londoners in
bleak clothes living bleak lives inherently

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:37.840
unsettling?

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:42.260
Probably that, although blood-hungry monsters,
freaky islands, and blood cults are scary

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:43.260
too.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.860
Fortunately, Apostle possesses all those things.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:50.850
Set in 1905, Apostle concerns a man named
Thomas, who leaves London for an island run

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:53.350
by a cult that's kidnapped his sister.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:57.300
Thomas poses as a new adherent to gain favor
with the cult members and their leader, in

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.410
the hopes of rescuing his sister from them.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:03.440
However, things get awfully sticky for Thomas
when he realizes that the cult's teachings

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.280
aren't exactly wrong.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:09.930
Imagine if Little Shop of Horrors mashed up
with The Wicker Man, only ten times as freaky,

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.760
and you'll get Apostle.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:17.440
There's always room for a new twist and new
voices in even the most trope-heavy film genres.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:21.940
Take Cargo, which revives the zombie movie
genre from its funk by adding new dimensions

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:23.150
of humanity.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:28.350
Directors Yolanda Ramke and Ben Howling based
the film on their 2013 short of the same name.

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:33.250
It follows a man named Andy, played by Martin
Freeman, who, with his wife and infant daughter,

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:37.520
preserves himself up in a houseboat along
a river deep in the interior of Australia

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.300
following a zombie apocalypse.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:43.890
Andy wants to take the boat upriver to the
safety of military protection; his wife wants

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:45.430
to make a supply run.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:50.140
Eventually, Andy heads out on land with Rosie
strapped to his back, fighting off the undead.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:55.310
Ultimately, Cargo is a film about the will
to not just survive, but to protect your loved

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.760
ones, no matter the cost.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:04.000
I Am Mother, the feature debut by writer-director
Grant Sputore, takes place after an apocalyptic,

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.840
extinction-level event has wiped out all of
humanity.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:11.750
Fortunately, a repopulation contingency plan
springs into action: a robot named Mother

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:18.030
activates in a secure lab facility and raises
one of 63,000 human embryos pre-frozen by

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:20.950
scientists should life ever cease to exist.

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:26.420
Mother then raises her human daughter, helpfully
named Daughter, through a pleasant childhood…until

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.480
things get prickly during the teen years.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:33.099
Daughter discovers a living mouse and wonders
if there's more life beyond her four walls.

00:08:33.099 --> 00:08:37.800
But then she finds out there really is, when
an adult human woman comes knocking at the

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:38.999
facility door.

00:08:38.999 --> 00:08:44.850
I Am Mother is ultimately a thrilling, chilling,
and even oddly touching allegory about parenthood

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:45.840
and letting go.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:51.440
The Wandering Earth is one of the highest-grossing
movies of the decade…but most North American

00:08:51.449 --> 00:08:54.680
movie fans probably have no idea it even exists.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:09:00.339
It enjoyed an extremely small release in the
U.S., but earned nearly $700 million at China's

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:01.339
box office.

00:09:01.339 --> 00:09:06.889
The film is one of that country's first Hollywood-style,
big-budget, blockbuster science-fiction epics.

00:09:06.889 --> 00:09:11.509
In The Wandering Earth, scientists discover
that the sun is evolving into a red giant,

00:09:11.509 --> 00:09:16.050
meaning that it's expanding at a rate that
will devour Earth in 100 years and the entire

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.439
solar system within 300 years.

00:09:18.439 --> 00:09:22.769
The globe's governments and scientists work
together and come up with a creative solution:

00:09:22.769 --> 00:09:27.999
10,000 gigantic jet engines are installed
around the world, propelling the planet out

00:09:27.999 --> 00:09:32.759
of its orbit to begin a very long journey
to a new permanent resting spot more than

00:09:32.759 --> 00:09:34.269
four lightyears away.

00:09:34.269 --> 00:09:38.800
Things go wrong relatively early when spaceship
Earth gets caught in Jupiter's orbit, which

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:43.471
will ensure its eventual destruction, if our
heroes can't get the jets working again, that

00:09:43.471 --> 00:09:44.471
is.

00:09:44.471 --> 00:09:50.329
Comparable to Armageddon, The Core, and Interstellar,
The Wandering Earth is a fun and accessible

00:09:50.329 --> 00:09:51.800
sci-fi adventure.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:57.080
Filmmakers can use the limitless tools and
imagination of science fiction to say something

00:09:57.089 --> 00:10:02.350
about the world, and Stefon Bristol explores
some powerful themes with See You Yesterday.

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:07.069
Bristol and his talented young cast combine
sci-fi tropes with brutal social commentary,

00:10:07.069 --> 00:10:12.350
this time-travel thriller is about the future
and the past, but really it's about the present.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:17.399
C.J., played by Eden Duncan-Smith, is a precocious
and preternaturally gifted young scientist

00:10:17.399 --> 00:10:21.870
who, with her best friend and collaborator
Sebastian, has constructed a rudimentary,

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:23.379
but functional, time machine.

00:10:23.379 --> 00:10:28.390
They just want to go back in time by a day
to look around and then come back, so as not

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:31.089
to "butterfly effect" the past and rewrite
history.

00:10:31.089 --> 00:10:35.660
But See You Yesterday is set in the predominantly
African-American Brooklyn neighborhood of

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:40.260
Flatbush, and C.J's brother Calvin is horrifyingly
shot down in the street by the police.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:44.899
C.J. has to use her device to go back and
attempt to save her brother's life while battling

00:10:44.899 --> 00:10:49.350
against the the time loops and complications
she both causes and encounters.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:54.079
See You Yesterday is a heartbreaking, thoughtful
movie, one that's laced with great sci-fi

00:10:54.079 --> 00:10:58.160
references as well as the Jamaican influence
that permeates Flatbush culture.

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:00.860
Don't waste anymore time, see this movie.

